WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:01.000
Silo: prepare your development sandbox.

00:01.000 --> 00:05.000
Choose which GitHub repositories a sandbox can access.

00:05.000 --> 00:08.000
Assign an API secret to a sandbox and an allowed HTTPS domain.

00:08.000 --> 00:10.000
Back up a local sandbox to an archive.

00:10.000 --> 00:12.000
Enable remote management on Office Mac.

00:12.000 --> 00:15.000
Connect Office Mac from the laptop. Its sandbox joins the local list.

00:15.000 --> 00:20.000
Start the remote sandbox from the laptop. Its status updates on both computers.

00:20.000 --> 00:22.000
Run a development server in the sandbox's terminal.

00:22.000 --> 00:26.500
Connect the discovered port in Network and open the site in a local browser.

00:26.500 --> 00:33.000
Enable SSH for the sandbox. Copy its address and save a connection key.

00:33.000 --> 00:40.000
Add the SSH connection to an illustrated coding agent on the laptop.

00:40.000 --> 00:46.500
Choose the project and submit a prompt. The agent reads files in the remote sandbox.

00:46.500 --> 00:47.500
Silo. Your tools here. Your sandbox there.
